  'lx.bombuse': 'A bomb takes the lead back. You have few of them, so timing decides games.\nUse one without hesitation when an opponent is about to go out; never on small early cards or on your partner.', 'lt.bombuse': 'Keeping one for your final move makes it much easier to go out.',
  'lx.trib': 'From the second hand on, the last player of the previous hand gives the winner their strongest card (not a ★ — a heart of the level). The winner gives back a card of 10 or lower.\nIf one team came 3rd and 4th (double down) both pay; whoever holds both big jokers pays nothing (anti-tribute).', 'lt.trib': 'Strongest means: big joker, small joker, level card, A …',
  'lx.up': 'The team that comes 1st moves up: +3 if the partner is 2nd, +2 if 3rd, +1 if 4th.\nIn a hand at level A you win the match by coming 1st with your partner not last. Fail three times at A and you drop back to 2.', 'lt.up': 'If the opponents come 1st, your level does not move.',
  'lx.lead': 'When everyone passes, the last player leads next. If that player has gone out, their partner opposite leads (catching the wind).\nA hand starts with the player who paid the tribute (with two tributes, the one who gave the bigger card). After an anti-tribute the previous winner leads.', 'lt.lead': 'Catching the wind helps your partner: leave them a shape they can follow.',
  'q.combos': 'Which shape is this?', 'q.compare': 'Which is stronger?', 'q.seqok': 'Can these cards be played as one combination?', 'q.wild': 'At level {l}, which card does the ★ stand for?', 'q.level': 'At level {l}, which is the strongest single?',
  'q.legal': 'Which of these can you play?', 'q.turns': 'In how few plays can this hand go out?', 'q.trib': 'At level {l}, which card must you give as tribute?', 'q.ret': 'Which card may be returned?', 'q.up': '{o}. How many levels does your team gain?', 'q.upA': 'Your team plays at level A and comes {r}. What happens?',
  'q.p.pass': 'Your partner {m} played a single {r}. Both opponents still have {n}+ cards. You hold an A…', 'q.p.feed': 'You lead. Your partner {m} has 1 card left; the opponents have many. What do you lead?', 'q.p.block': 'You lead. {o}, the opponent who plays next, has 1 card left. What do you lead?',
  'q.b.stop': 'Opponent {o} ({n} cards left) played a {c}. Only a bomb of yours beats it. What do you do?', 'q.b.wait': 'Early in the hand, opponent {o} ({n} cards left) plays a single {r}. You hold a bomb and a K.', 'q.b.mate': 'Your partner {m}\'s play is on the table and the opponents passed. You hold a bomb.',
  'q.l.last': 'Everyone passed on {n}\'s play. Who leads next?', 'q.l.out': '{n} played their last cards and went out; everyone else passed. Who leads next?', 'q.l.trib': '{g}, last in the previous hand, gave you (1st) a tribute. Who leads first this hand?', 'q.l.anti': '{g}, last in the previous hand, holds both big jokers: anti-tribute (you were 1st). Who leads first?',
  'lq.yes': 'Yes', 'lq.no': 'No', 'lq.none': 'Not a combination', 'lq.o.pass': 'Pass and leave it to your partner', 'lq.o.over': 'Play the A and take it', 'lq.o.low': 'Your lowest single', 'lq.o.high': 'Your strongest card', 'lq.o.pair': 'A pair (not a single)',
  'lq.o.bomb': 'Use the bomb', 'lq.o.small': 'Play the K (keep the bomb)', 'lq.o.none': 'No change', 'lq.o.winM': 'You win the match', 'lq.o.stayA': 'Still A (one failure)', 'lq.o13': '1st and 3rd', 'lq.o14': '1st and 4th', 'lq.o12': '1st and 2nd',
  'e.none': 'A 6-card straight, two pairs or J-Q-K-A-2 fit none of the shapes, so they cannot be played.',
  'e.ct.pair': 'Two of a rank: a pair.', 'e.ct.triple': 'Three of a rank: a triple.', 'e.ct.full': 'A triple plus a pair: a full house.', 'e.ct.straight': 'Five in a row, mixed suits: a straight.', 'e.ct.tube': 'Three consecutive pairs.', 'e.ct.plate': 'Two consecutive triples.', 'e.ct.bomb': 'Four or more of a rank: a bomb.', 'e.ct.sflush': 'Five in a row in one suit: a straight flush (a kind of bomb).',
  'e.cmp.set': 'The higher rank wins ({r}).', 'e.cmp.full': 'A full house is compared by its triple only ({r} is higher).', 'e.cmp.seq': 'Runs compare by their top card.', 'e.cmp.lvl': 'At level {l}, {l} beats A.',
  'e.seqA.low': 'A run starting with A (A2345 …) counts the A as 1: it is the lowest run.', 'e.seqA.wrap': 'A run cannot wrap around A (K-A-2).', 'e.seqA.ok': 'A proper run: {c}.',
  'e.wild': 'The ★ stands for the {r} and completes the run.', 'e.level': 'At level {l}, {l} beats A — but not the jokers.', 'e.level.j': 'A joker is stronger than the level cards.',
